      <h2 id="how-we-evaluated">How We Evaluated</h2>
      <p>We evaluated CRM software based on vendor documentation, pricing pages, public feature comparisons, administrator and sales operations community discussions, and migration case studies. Each CRM was assessed following the <a href="/how-we-test/">ToolStep review protocol</a> — focusing on onboarding time to first usable pipeline, breadth and quality of the free tier, automation capability without code, reporting depth, integration coverage, and cost per seat at 10, 50, and 200 users.</p>

      <h2 id="ranking-methodology">Ranking Methodology</h2>
      <p>Weighted scoring across six CRM evaluation dimensions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Ease of Onboarding (25%)</strong> — Time from signup to first deal stage, reliance on consulting or admin, and end-user adoption friction</li>
        <li><strong>Pricing &amp; Tiers (20%)</strong> — Free tier quality, entry price, professional/enterprise pricing jumps, and total cost at 10/50/200 seats</li>
        <li><strong>Automation (20%)</strong> — Workflow builders, process automation, scheduled actions, and code-level automation capability</li>
        <li><strong>Customization (15%)</strong> — Custom fields, custom objects, layouts, record types, and permissions</li>
        <li><strong>Reporting &amp; Analytics (10%)</strong> — Pipeline reports, dashboards, forecasting, and AI analytics</li>
        <li><strong>Integrations &amp; Ecosystem (10%)</strong> — Marketplace size, native integrations, API and webhook access</li>
      </ul>

